Harmattan: a position plugin for Nokia's positioningd

The phone has no GeoClue: positions come from positioningd on the session bus
(com.nokia.positioningd.client), as they did for Qt Mobility's maemo backend
(dbuscomm_maemo.cpp, dbusserver_maemo.cpp). Each source registers a listener
(registerListener(service, path) -> id, methods, minimum interval) under its own bus name,
com.nokia.qlocation.I<uuid>, and drives its session with configSession(id, command, method,
interval): start/stop, satellites start/stop, methods, interval. The daemon calls back
com.nokia.qlocation.updates (positionUpdate, satellitesInViewUpdate, satellitesInUseUpdate:
QDataStream bytes of Qt Mobility's types, Qt 4.7's stream version; currentSettings);
calls from anyone but the daemon we registered with are ignored.

Both position and satellite sources; area monitoring comes from positionpoll. The daemon's
D-Bus policy (/etc/dbus-1/session.d/aegis.positioningd.conf) lets only processes with Aegis'
Location credential call it: without it the sources report AccessError. On this mkspec the
plugin replaces the two GeoClue ones.

